<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sho Tai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1843">1843</a>–<a href="/years/1901">1901</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sho Tai was the last king of the Ryukyu Kingdom, reigning from 1848 to 1879. Meiji <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> made him lord of the Ryukyu Domain in 1872 and, when the domain was abolished and annexed as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/okinawa-prefecture">Okinawa Prefecture</a> in 1879, removed him to Tokyo, where he was made a marquis in the Japanese peerage. He died in 1901.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sho-tai.jpg" alt="Sho Tai" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sho_Tai.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
